commit 4fce662163a1f7e867eee55e37a84f6fa663e00e
Author: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 7 12:34:10 2026 -0700

    Put every Agent panel corner back on the radius scale

    The panel's stylesheet carried radii the design system does not define. The
    scale is 6, 8, and 12; the panel used 4 in eleven places, 10 in one, and the
    unnamed 999 in three.

    Eleven 4px radii become 6. These are standard controls and small surfaces --
    the base button rule, the composer textarea, the chat dialog input, the icon
    and attach buttons, the image thumbnail, and the mono blocks that hold code
    and hashes. Four was the standard radius until it moved to 6, so these were
    correct when written and drifted when the token changed rather than through
    any local mistake. The attachment chips were already 6, which is why the
    composer looked subtly mismatched: chips at 6 sitting beside buttons at 4.

    The setup card moves 10 -> 12. It is a large surface, not a control, so it
    takes radius/window; 8 would have made it read like the compact controls
    sitting inside it.

    The three capsules -- history status, agent badge, setup progress -- keep
    their shape but stop being a magic number. radius/pill is added to
    design-tokens.json and declared once in the stylesheet. Colour tokens reach
    the page through tokens.ts at runtime, but dimension tokens are not plumbed
    that way at all, so the value is declared in CSS and mirrored in the token
    file rather than read from it.

    Menu rows stay a radius rather than going to 0. The native rule, until now
    recorded only in a comment in Shell/HeaderControls.cpp, is that rows carry no
    radius because they run the full width of an already-rounded popover. The
    panel's menu pads its rows by 4px, so they are inset controls and the rule
    does not apply. That rule and the capsule are both written into
    design-system.md so the next person does not have to read C++ to find them.

    Verified: 65 tests pass; before/after screenshots of the chat, chat list,
    setup chooser, tool list, diff, and progress screens show no layout shift.

    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M1YNT8Y4SAHV5DVYWVQJ6VXA

