commit cd353772cbd312415da2243aa20ddf27d0a19ea5
Author: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 7 12:40:34 2026 -0700

    Put the Agent panel's type back on the role scale

    The panel used sizes the design system does not define: 13px in ten places,
    11px in four, and 16px in two. The roles are page title 24/30, section 18/24,
    body and control 14/20, label 12/16 bold, and dense metadata 10/14. Every
    size below moves with its line height, since changing one without the other
    looks worse than leaving both alone.

    Every 13px becomes Body 14/20. All ten were running text, control text, or
    preformatted content the reader is meant to read: the base button rule, chat
    list titles, the Configure Agent label, dialog copy, pane-state copy, the
    setup tool rows, the copyable setup command, the settings diff, and the list
    of what setup will do. None was metadata, so Label was never the answer.

    Every 11px becomes Dense Metadata 10/14 -- chat list timestamps, the
    Configure Agent subtitle, the build provenance line, and the setup footnote.
    These are annotations, and 12 was not available to them: Label is defined as
    bold, and all four are regular weight.

    One 11px does not follow that rule. Build warnings shared a declaration with
    the provenance line, so the brief counted them as one decision, but they are
    not the same role: a slice warning is the most actionable line on the card
    and should not shrink below the metadata around it. It is split out to Label
    12/16 bold, which is both a defined role and the right emphasis.

    Both 16px headings become Section 18/24. This collapses markdown h1 and h2
    into one size, because the scale offers nothing between 18 and 14; the
    alternative collapsed h2 into h3 instead. Headings render at heading size,
    which is the better of the two.

    The remaining off-scale numbers are the 20px '+' and 16px 'x' glyphs on the
    composer's attach and remove buttons. These are icons expressed as text, and
    16, 20, and 24 are all valid functional icon sizes, so they are already on a
    scale -- just not the type one. Drawing them as SVG is a component change,
    not a token one, and is left alone.

    Verified: 65 tests pass. Before/after screenshots of the chat, chat list,
    setup chooser, tool list, settings diff, and progress screens show the panel
    one pixel shorter overall -- the 13->14 growth and the 11->10 shrink cancel.
    The one visible density change is the settings diff, which grows about 74px
    and wraps the helper path onto a third line; that screen is where the user
    reviews what JusPrin will write to their filesystem, so body size is right
    for it.

    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M1YP60DN8J41NZ9T4BG3CQ0D

